Tech Stack
	•	Google Colab: Enables interactive cloud-based Python notebooks for data analysis, preprocessing, and model development.
	•	Gemini: Used for advanced AI-powered modeling, experimentation, and deployment workflows.

Libraries Used
	•	pandas: Data manipulation and cleaning, DataFrame creation, and handling missing values.
	•	geopy.distance (geodesic): Calculating geodesic (straight-line on Earth’s surface) distances between latitude/longitude coordinates.
	•	numpy: Array operations, calculating medians for missing value imputation, basic numerical computations.
	•	joblib: Saving and loading trained machine learning models efficiently.



Data Pipeline Overview
1. Data Loading
	•	Load the `data.csv` dataset into a Pandas DataFrame.
2. Data Cleaning & Preprocessing
	•	Extract latitude and longitude values from `org_lat_lon` and `des_lat_lon`.
	•	Convert latitude/longitude columns to numeric types.
	•	Remove rows with invalid coordinate values.
	•	Handle missing values (using median/mode imputation or by dropping rows/columns as appropriate).
	•	Recalculate `trip_duration_seconds_recalculated` and `delay_seconds_recalculated` based on start/end timestamps.
	•	Drop original time delta fields and unnecessary time-only columns.
	•	Handle outliers (rows dropped in current version, though in production these may be flagged or transformed).
	•	Remove irrelevant columns.
3. Models Used To Determine Baseline To Achieve High Scores
  - Linear Regression
  - Random Forest
  - Gradient Boosting Regressor
  - K NeighborsRegressor 

