5. Feature Engineering
	•	Derive temporal features: `start_hour`, `start_day_of_week`, `end_hour`, `end_day_of_week`.
	•	Create categorical features such as `trip_duration_category` (if relevant to modeling).
	•	Generate interaction features (e.g., `vehicle_type_x_distance`, `start_hour_x_day_of_week`) shown to improve model performance.
6. Categorical Encoding
	•	Apply One-Hot Encoding to selected categorical columns.
7. Model Training (for reproducibility)
	•	Define model architectures and tuned hyperparameters.
	•	While training is not done in production, this ensures models can be reloaded consistently.
	•	Trained models should be serialized and saved for downstream use.
8. Prediction
	•	Load the trained models and run prediction on new trip records.
